<title>FRANCE: French pensions bill due for final adoption Thurs.</title>
<headline>French pensions bill due for final adoption Thurs.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>A bill introducing pension funds to France is scheduled for definitive adoption in the upper and lower houses of parliament on Thursday, according to parliamentary papers.</p>
<p>The Senate, the upper house of parliament, will vote on the final text of the bill at 0800 GMT and the National Assembly, the lower house, will vote at 1400 GMT.</p>
<p>The government has said it wants to introduce private pension funds to complement the existing system of universal pensions, boost the stock market and bolster company capital. However, opposition Socialists, who fear any dismantling of France's welfare state. have criticised the plan and have vowed to challenge the bill in the Constitutional Court.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
</text>
